   "fen": "r1b1kb1r/1p1n1ppp/p3pn2/2pq4/2NP4/2P2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 2 8",
   "line": [
    "Nbd7"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black defends the b6-square the right way — with the knight to d7, guarding while developing. Both jobs in one move.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Meet a positional threat with a move that also develops, not a passive pawn move.",
   "plans": "(For White:) restrict with a4 and keep squeezing."
